  "prefLabel": "Rev 901.06 Corporation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 901.06 “Corporation” means an artificial person or legal entity created under the laws of incorporation of any state or foreign country without recognizing the distinctions between types of corporations such as those drawn in the IRC between S corporations and other corporations.\n\nSource. #4557, eff 12-28-88; ss by #5947, eff 12-29-94; ss by #6321, eff 8-22-96; ss by #8137, eff 8-10-04; ss by #9658, eff 2-24-10; ss by #9843, eff 12-23-10 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rev 900); ss by #10211, eff 10-24-12; renumbered by #10795 (from Rev 901.05); ss by #13433, eff 8-12-22",
